  "body": "From #96. The new vertical-rapid law reads stock as columns from above (world Z), which on a lathe is the spindle axis - the column beside the bar is solid all the way down, so it cannot see what the part or earlier passes removed. #96 therefore drops RapidInStock for turning ops' rapids along the axis (crates/app/src/operation/turning_rapids.rs). Those rapids were never checked before #96 either (every vertical rapid was skipped), so nothing regressed - but a turning rapid along Z into the bar is still unwatched.\n\nDone means: turning rapids along the axis are judged in the turning (meridian) plane against the revolved stock and the material earlier passes removed, blocking the post when one enters uncut stock; the turning_rapids exemption removed; pinned by a lathe fixture whose axial rapid enters the bar.",
